{% extends 'layouts/page.njk' %}

{% block content %}
  {{ appHeading({
    text: heading,
    caption: "apha-incubator-frontend-poc"
  }) }}

  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <div class="govuk-body" data-testid="app-page-body">
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Charting library prototypes</h2>
        <p>
          Three dashboard prototypes render the same four charts from the same synthetic
          animal disease outbreak dataset, each using a different charting library. They exist
          so the libraries can be compared like for like against GOV.UK Design System and
          accessibility expectations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each dashboard shows weekly new cases, cases by region, cases by disease and a
          severity breakdown. Every chart is paired with an accessible data table, and the
          weekly new cases chart opens an expanded, filterable view.
        </p>

        <ul class="govuk-list" data-testid="prototype-links">
          {% for prototype in prototypes %}
            <li class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-3">
              <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ prototype.href }}">{{ prototype.name }} dashboard</a>
              <br>
              <span class="govuk-hint">{{ prototype.description }}</span>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <p class="govuk-hint">
          The prototypes are delivered on separate branches, so a link will only work once
          that branch is merged.
        </p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Live data</h2>
        <p>
          <a class="govuk-link" href="/latest-cases">Latest cases</a>
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-hint">
          Avian influenza events in Europe reported to WOAH's WAHIS in the last 24 hours,
          pulled live from the public WAHIS API.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

{% endblock %}
